<title>FRANCE: Publicis buys two Israeli ad agencies.</title>
<headline>Publicis buys two Israeli ad agencies.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>French advertising firm Publicis S.A. said on Tuesday it had signed two separate accords giving the group a 51 percent majority stake and control of the Israeli Ariely and Pelled agencies.</p>
<p>&quot;These two aquisitions give the Publicis group leading rank in Israel,&quot; Publicis head Maurice Levy said in a statement.</p>
<p>Ariely Advertising Ltd, which is traded on Nasdaq, had billings of $38 million in 1996, will be called Publicis Ariely.</p>
<p>Pelled had billings of $18 million in 1996.</p>
</text>
